# Maps the several identities people have committed under onto one each, so
# `git shortlog`, `git log --author` and anything counting contributions see a
# person rather than an address.
#
# Format: canonical name and address first, then the variant being folded into
# it. Nothing here rewrites history — it is a lookup table git applies when it
# displays an author.

# Two machines, one person: an early series of commits carries the hostname the
# work was done on rather than a real address.
Lars Vonhof-Hunold <lars@vonhof-hunold.de> Lars <lhuno@vserver19.panxatony.net>

# Schlaefer used two addresses of the same mailbox across the years.
Schlaefer <openmail+sourcecode@siezi.com> <openmail+github@siezi.com>
